@62 = ~Astarion's Dangerous Bargain~
@63 = ~I agreed to Astarion's bargain. He wants us to kill an art dealer named Derek in Baldur's Gate and return with his body in exchange for 6,000 gold pieces. Derek is said to live near the Silvershield estate.~
@64 = ~I confronted Derek but decided to let him escape. I should return to Astarion and explain that I have no body to deliver.~
@65 = ~Derek paid us to let him go. He fled before we could fulfil Astarion's request. I should return to Astarion, though he may not appreciate this outcome.~
@66 = ~I returned to Astarion with Derek's body. Instead of paying as promised, he revealed that the bargain had been a trap and attacked us.~
@67 = ~Derek escaped. When I reported this to Astarion, he claimed Derek had already been dealt with, and turned on us. The bargain is finished.~
@68 = ~I refused to continue working for Astarion. He became hostile, ending our bargain.~
